            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 44,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this something you want the bmcweb change to go first for?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 44,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't have a bmcweb change ready yet, but lets not wait.   Worst case you see \"UNAVAILABLE\" show up in an API for a moment until we (I) fix it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 44,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "FWIW, I typed this up quickly.  I'm wondering if \"NOT_SUPPORTED\" might be a better tombstone value.  UNAVAILBLE might imply temporarily unavailable and get accidentally used.\n\nStill thinking about it.  will ping discord for more input."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Asset.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I assume we should just apply this to everything in Inventory?  Should we put it in a README.md under yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Asset.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "That's probably a better idea than whats here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Asset.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Patch has been moved to a new README.md"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Asset.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Interestingly in some cases we already have \"default\" values like this empty string here.  I guess we should probably change all the default values to UNAVAILABLE for every single string?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Asset.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "That's probably a good idea."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Asset.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Should the default be left as empty string, so that from the code end a property read can be simply checked for empty() to detect if the value is available or not instead of going for a string comparison with \"UNAVAILABLE\", also it will not affect any existing code if there is a check for empty string to detect unavailability of value. And explicit handling in code can be done to check for property value \"UNPOPULATED\"?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Asset.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> if there is a check for empty string to detect unavailability of value\n\nFrom what I've seen it's the opposite, empty string seems to be for \"Allowed but unpopulated\".\n\nAt an interface level, we need to break someone, I'd rather break the case where the alternative is just not being supported at all (ie, nobody can ever use it) rather than try to change the default on the case that people use and expect to work."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Asset.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm having trouble understanding the differentiation between \"unpopulated\" and \"unavailable\" in this case.  It seems like we either get the EEPROM or we don't; if we don't have it, the whole device is going to not show up.  An \"unpopulated\" field is one where the EEPROM is empty (or doesn't provide that information).\n\nIs there some additional case of \"unavailable\" that I'm missing?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Asset.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "> I'm having trouble understanding the differentiation between \"unpopulated\" and \"unavailable\" in this case. \n\nMy point was to not replace the default(which is empty string currently) with \"unavailable\" as proposed in the chain above to avoid any code breaks, instead have value set as \"unpopulated\" to reflect the state where there is an access error or error in fetching these values. \nHaving said that, I agree with what @ed@tanous.net has mentioned here.\n\n> if we don't have it, the whole device is going to not show up\n\nTrue but we have some use cases where we publish inventory paths even for FRUs which are not present with \"Present=false\" and rest of the interfaces with default values.\nAnyways those are specific use cases so we can skip that here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Asset.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> It seems like we either get the EEPROM or we don't\n\nIf only the world were that simple \ud83d\ude0a. If we limit ourselves to only IPMI FRU a field might be present, but empty string (sub types might be all zeros or length 0, the former is common but not in the spec), not present, or populated.\n\n> An \"unpopulated\" field is one where the EEPROM is empty (or doesn't provide that information).\n\nThis is the problem, we need to differentiate those two cases, because a field that's empty can be written or updated, and needs to be shown as empty string or null in Redfish (to denote its writability)  A field that's not present at all can't be written, and can't be included in Redfish.\n\nExpanding out to things that aren't IPMI FRUs like pirom, custom fru formats, or devices that directly support commands to identify themselves (like Intel ME) these fields might not exist at all, and shouldn't be populated as empty string in Redfish."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Asset.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I've changed this to NOTSUPPORTED."
                }
            ],
